From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: blurbery <271863866+blurbery@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_avfoundation: build for iOS and tvOS

The AVFoundation audio output already sets up AVAudioSession on iOS and
tvOS, but it does not compile there: with HAVE_AVFOUNDATION the CoreAudio
helpers declare and build the macOS-only HAL functions (AudioDeviceID,
AudioStreamID, AudioObject), and init() selects an output device through
setAudioOutputDeviceUniqueID:, which iOS and tvOS do not have.

Add CA_HAVE_HAL, true for the CoreAudio output and for AVFoundation on
macOS, and use it in place of HAVE_COREAUDIO || HAVE_AVFOUNDATION. On iOS
and tvOS the AVFoundation output then has no device list or device
selection and uses the shared AVAudioSession route, as the AudioUnit
output does. macOS builds are unchanged. Applies to mpv v0.41.0.

Licence: this patch is part of Vivid's Lucid Engine patch series for mpv.
